), with the increase of diffraction angle, the d value decreases and the cell volume decreases. In the above cases, the partial replacement of O2– (radius-140 pm) of C3S by F- (radius-136 pm) [37] and the partial substitution of Ca2+ (radius-99 pm) of C3S by Cu2+ (radius-76 pm) might result in the decrease of C3S cell structure [51].
